NAMING_VS_MECHANISM:
Mostly RE-APPLICATION, with a narrow real delta. The "correctness-safety break-even map" is a re-skin of the standard speculation cost model (Leviathan; branch-prediction theory): p*=penalty/(gain+penalty) is textbook. The latency OVERLAP is known practice (authors concede this). The genuine MECHANISM delta is two-fold and narrow: (1) the substrate — committing on a partial TOOL-RESULT stream rather than a token draft or a tool call; (2) the empirical detectability-necessity finding (BLIND-detector ablation: 242/540 cells win, −57% worst-case) which makes "partial-stream detectability" a load-bearing precondition rather than a free assumption. That detectability-as-precondition framing for semantic tool-result early-commit is something I could NOT match to a published source — but with live search blocked I cannot certify it as novel either.

